$$************************************************************************************************** 
************************************** GENERAL INFORMATION *****************************************
****************************************************************************************************

Script for calculating a phase diagram in a binary system according to Tutorial 8.
The following contents will be covered:

 - Calculating phase boundaries
 - Building up the phase diagram from the calculated boundaries
 - Choosing appropriate calculation parameters
 - Phase diagrams using stable and metastable equilibria

A phase diagram consists of a number of phase-boundaries separating regions of temperature- and 
composition-space in which different phases are stable at equilibrium. Published equilibrium 
diagrams for the Fe-C system often show equilibria between Fe-rich phases and both C (in the form
of graphite) and cementite (Fe3C). Graphite is the more stable of these two phases, and forms 
readily in cast irons (2-4 wt.% C), but usually with great difficulty in steels (up to 1.5 wt.% C).
In the latter, it is more practically useful to consider metastable equilibria involving Fe3C. 
In this tutorial, phase diagrams for both Fe-C and Fe-Fe3C will be calculated.

Database: mc_fe.tdb
Author: P. Warczok
Creation date: 10.11.2008
Last update: 15.05.2019 (P. Warczok, Update for 6.02)
This is a script for MatCalc version 6.02 (rel 1.003)

Known issues:
- "save-workspace "file-name"=Tutorial_8" is not working properly. Use "save-workspace Tutorial_8" instead.
- Dependent phase for the stepped calculation of "phase boundary" type can be defined either by 
  "set-step-option scheil-dependent-phase=" or by "set-step-option T0-dependent-phase=", though this is not
  "Scheil" or "T0" calculation... Still, both of these seem to work fine in this role as well. 



**************************************************************************************************** 
************************************** SETUP INFORMATION *******************************************
**************************************************************************************************$$

use-module module-name=core  $ Use "core" module (MatCalc uses "core" module by default anyway) 

new-workspace $ creates a new workspace 


$$************************************************************************************************** 
**************************************** SYSTEM SETUP **********************************************
**************************************************************************************************$$



$$************************************************************************************************** 
                        DATABASES, CHEMICAL COMPOSITION, SELECTED PHASES
**************************************************************************************************$$

open-thermodynamic-database file-name=mc_fe.tdb                                                $ Thermodynamic database: mc_fe.tdb
select-elements elements=FE C VA                                                               $ Components: Fe, C
select-phases phases=LIQUID FCC_A1 BCC_A2 CEMENTITE GRAPHITE                                   $ Phase selection
read-thermodynamic-database 

set-reference-element element=FE
enter-composition type=weight-percent composition=C=0,05                                       $ Composition: 0.05 wt.% C

set-automatic-startvalues
set-temperature-celsius temperature=1000                                                       $ Temperature 1000C
calculate-equilibrium                                                                          $ Initial equilibrium

new-gui-window type-id=p1                                                                      $ Plot of the phase diagram

$ Suspend graphite phase
change-phase-status phase-name=graphite set-flag=suspended 


$$************************************************************************************************** 
                                       FE-FE3C PHASE DIAGRAM
**************************************************************************************************$$

$-------------------------------- Upper boundary of delta-ferrite ---------------------------------$
set-temperature-celsius temperature=1530                                                       $ Temperature 1530C
calculate-equilibrium
search-phase-boundary phase-name=BCC_A2 temperature                                            $ Varying temperature for the phase boundary search		

set-step-option type=phase-boundary                                                            $ "Phase boundary" type
set-step-option scheil-dependent-phase=BCC_A2                                                  $ Phase boundary of bcc phase field
set-step-option element=C                                                                      $ Carbon content varied
set-step-option range start=0 stop=5 scale=lin step-width=0.01                                 $ Range 0 - 5; linear step of 0,01
set-step-option element-content-in-wt%=yes                                                     $ Composition in wt.%
set-step-option temperature-in-celsius=yes                                                     $ Temperature in Celsius
set-step-option maximum-temperature-step=20                                                    $ Setting the max. T-step to 20
step-equilibrium

set-plot-option plot-id=. series new buffer variable-name=T$C                                  $ Plotting the phase boundary
$ Display major grid lines for x-axis
set-plot-option plot-id=. grid which-grid=major enable-x-axis=yes 
$ Display major grid lines for y-axis
set-plot-option plot-id=. grid which-grid=major enable-y-axis=yes 
$ Duplicate and lock all (unlocked) series 
set-gui-window-property window-id=. duplicate-and-lock-plot-series 
$ Renaming series: "*_T$C" --> "bcc_high_1"
set-plot-option plot-id=. series rename series-index=-1 series-name=*_T$C new-name=bcc_high_1


$---------------------------------- Lower boundary of liquid --------------------------------------$
set-temperature-celsius temperature=1500                                                        $ Temperature 1500C
calculate-equilibrium 
search-phase-boundary phase-name=LIQUID temperature                                             $ Varying temperature for the phase boundary search

set-step-option type=phase-boundary                                                             $ "Phase boundary" type
set-step-option scheil-dependent-phase=LIQUID                                                   $ Phase boundary of liquid phase field
set-step-option element=C                                                                       $ Carbon content varied
set-step-option range start=0 stop=5 scale=lin step-width=0.01                                  $ Range 0 - 5; linear step of 0,01
set-step-option element-content-in-wt%=yes                                                      $ Composition in wt.%
set-step-option temperature-in-celsius=yes                                                      $ Temperature in C
set-step-option maximum-temperature-step=20                                                     $ Setting the max. T-step to 20
step-equilibrium

$ Duplicate and lock all unlocked series 
set-gui-window-property window-id=. duplicate-and-lock-plot-series
set-plot-option plot-id=. series rename series-index=-1 series-name=*_T$C new-name=liquid       $ Renaming series: "*_T$C" --> "liquid"


$------------------------------- Lower boundary of delta-ferrite ----------------------------------$
set-temperature-celsius temperature=1400                                                        $ Temperature 1400C
calculate-equilibrium
search-phase-boundary phase-name=BCC_A2 temperature                                             $ Varying temperature for the phase boundary search

set-step-option type=phase-boundary                                                             $ "Phase boundary" type
set-step-option scheil-dependent-phase=BCC_A2                                                   $ Phase boundary of bcc phase field
set-step-option element=C                                                                       $ Carbon content varied
set-step-option range start=0 stop=5 scale=lin step-width=0.01                                  $ Range 0 - 5; linear step of 0,01
set-step-option element-content-in-wt%=yes                                                      $ Composition in wt.%
set-step-option temperature-in-celsius=yes                                                      $ Temperature in Celsius
set-step-option maximum-temperature-step=20                                                     $ Setting the max. T-step to 20
step-equilibrium  

set-gui-window-property window-id=. duplicate-and-lock-plot-series                              $ Locking all unlocked series
set-plot-option plot-id=. series rename series-index=-1 series-name=*_T$C new-name=bcc_high_2   $ Renaming series: "*_T$C" --> "bcc_high_2"


$---------------------------------- Upper boundary of austenite -----------------------------------$
set-temperature-celsius temperature=1500                                                        $ Temperature 1500C
calculate-equilibrium
search-phase-boundary phase-name=FCC_A1 temperature                                             $ Varying temperature for the phase boundary search

set-step-option type=phase-boundary                                                             $ "Phase boundary" type
set-step-option scheil-dependent-phase=FCC_A1                                                   $ Phase boundary of fcc phase field
set-step-option element=C                                                                       $ Carbon content varied
set-step-option range start=0 stop=5 scale=lin step-width=0.01                                  $ Range 0 - 5; linear step of 0,01
set-step-option element-content-in-wt%=yes                                                      $ Composition in wt.%
set-step-option temperature-in-celsius=yes                                                      $ Temperature in Celsius
set-step-option maximum-temperature-step=20                                                     $ Setting the max. T-step to 20
step-equilibrium

set-gui-window-property window-id=. duplicate-and-lock-plot-series                              $ Locking all unlocked series
set-plot-option plot-id=. series rename series-index=-1 series-name=*_T$C new-name=fcc_1        $ Renaming series: "*_T$C" --> "fcc_1"


$-------------------------------- Upper boundary of alpha-ferrite ---------------------------------$
set-temperature-celsius temperature=900                                                         $ Temperature 900C
calculate-equilibrium
search-phase-boundary phase-name=BCC_A2 temperature                                             $ Varying temperature for the phase boundary search

set-step-option type=phase-boundary                                                             $ "Phase boundary" type
set-step-option scheil-dependent-phase=BCC_A2                                                   $ Phase boundary of bcc phase field
set-step-option element=C                                                                       $ Carbon content varied
set-step-option range start=0 stop=5 scale=lin step-width=0.01                                  $ Range 0 - 5; linear step of 0,01
set-step-option element-content-in-wt%=yes                                                      $ Composition in wt.%
set-step-option temperature-in-celsius=yes                                                      $ Temperature in Celsius
set-step-option maximum-temperature-step=20                                                     $ Setting the max. T-step to 20
step-equilibrium

set-gui-window-property window-id=. duplicate-and-lock-plot-series                              $ Locking all unlocked series
set-plot-option plot-id=. series rename series-index=-1 series-name=*_T$C new-name=bcc_low      $ Renaming series: "*_T$C" --> "bcc_low"


$--------------------------------- Lower boundary of austenite ------------------------------------$
set-temperature-celsius temperature=600                                                         $ Temperature 600C
calculate-equilibrium
search-phase-boundary phase-name=FCC_A1 temperature                                             $ Varying temperature for the phase boundary search

set-step-option type=phase-boundary                                                             $ "Phase boundary" type
set-step-option scheil-dependent-phase=FCC_A1                                                   $ Phase boundary of fcc phase field
set-step-option element=C                                                                       $ Carbon content varied
set-step-option range start=0 stop=5 scale=lin step-width=0.001                                 $ Range 0 - 5; linear step of 0,001
set-step-option element-content-in-wt%=yes                                                      $ Composition in wt.%
set-step-option temperature-in-celsius=yes                                                      $ Temperature in Celsius
set-step-option maximum-temperature-step=20                                                     $ Setting the max. T-step to 20
step-equilibrium

set-gui-window-property window-id=. duplicate-and-lock-plot-series                              $ Locking all unlocked series
set-plot-option plot-id=. series rename series-index=-1 series-name=*_T$C new-name=fcc_2        $ Renaming series: "*_T$C" --> "fcc_2"


$-------------------------------- Cementite upper phase boundary ----------------------------------$
set-temperature-celsius temperature=800                                                         $ Temperature 800C
calculate-equilibrium
search-phase-boundary phase-name=CEMENTITE temperature                                          $ Varying temperature for the phase boundary search

set-step-option type=phase-boundary                                                             $ "Phase boundary" type
set-step-option scheil-dependent-phase=CEMENTITE                                                $ Phase boundary of cementite phase field
set-step-option element=C                                                                       $ Carbon content varied
set-step-option range start=0 stop=5 scale=lin step-width=0.01                                  $ Range 0 - 5; linear step of 0,01
set-step-option element-content-in-wt%=yes                                                      $ Composition in wt.%
set-step-option temperature-in-celsius=yes                                                      $ Temperature in Celsius
set-step-option maximum-temperature-step=200                                                    $ Setting the max. T-step to 200
step-equilibrium

$ lock series "T$C"
set-plot-option plot-id=. series lock series-index=-1 series-name=T$C do-lock=yes 
set-plot-option plot-id=. series rename series-index=-1 series-name=*_T$C new-name=cementite    $ Renaming series: "*_T$C" --> "cementite"


$------------------------------------- The finished diagram ---------------------------------------$
$ Plot title. "<sub>" and "</sub>" are used to mark the text which should be written as a subscript
set-plot-option plot-id=. plot-title=Fe-Fe<sub>3</sub>C phase diagram
set-gui-window-property window-id=. default-x-axis-title=Carbon content [wt.%]                  $ x-axis title 
set-plot-option plot-id=. y-axis-title=Temperature [C]                                          $ y-axis title
$ Scaling of y-axis starts from "400"
set-plot-option plot-id=. y-axis-scaling=400..


$$************************************************************************************************** 
                                        FE-C PHASE DIAGRAM
**************************************************************************************************$$

$ Activate graphite again - remove "suspended" flag
change-phase-status phase-name=GRAPHITE clear-flag=suspended 
set-temperature-celsius temperature=1600                                                        $ Temperature 1600C
calculate-equilibrium

create-new-plot plot-type=xy-plot attach-to-window=.                                            $ Fe-C phase diagram will be drawn on the new plot
set-plot-option plot-id=. grid which-grid=major enable-x-axis=yes                               $ Switching on the major gridlines for x-axis
set-plot-option plot-id=. grid which-grid=major enable-y-axis=yes                               $ Switching on the major gridlines for y-axis

$------------------------------- Upper boundary of delta-ferrite ----------------------------------$
search-phase-boundary phase-name=BCC_A2 temperature                                             $ Varying temperature for the phase boundary search

set-step-option type=phase-boundary                                                             $ "Phase boundary" type
set-step-option scheil-dependent-phase=BCC_A2                                                   $ Phase boundary of bcc phase field
set-step-option element=C                                                                       $ Carbon content varied
set-step-option range start=0 stop=5 scale=lin step-width=0.01                                  $ Range 0 - 5; linear step of 0,01
set-step-option element-content-in-wt%=yes                                                      $ Composition in wt.%
set-step-option temperature-in-celsius=yes                                                      $ Temperature in Celsius
set-step-option maximum-temperature-step=20                                                     $ Setting the max. T-step to 20
step-equilibrium

set-plot-option plot-id=. series new buffer variable-name=T$C                                   $ Drawing the phase boundary in the new plot
set-gui-window-property window-id=. duplicate-and-lock-plot-series                              $ Locking all unlocked series
set-plot-option plot-id=. series rename series-index=-1 series-name=*_T$C new-name=bcc_high_1   $ Renaming series: "*_T$C" --> "bcc_high_1"


$----------------------------------- Lower boundary of liquid -------------------------------------$
set-temperature-celsius temperature=1500                                                        $ Temperature 1500C
calculate-equilibrium 
search-phase-boundary phase-name=LIQUID temperature                                             $ Varying temperature for the phase boundary search

set-step-option type=phase-boundary                                                             $ "Phase boundary" type
set-step-option scheil-dependent-phase=LIQUID                                                   $ Phase boundary of liquid phase field
